meta {
  name: Webhook
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/donate/webhook
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  x-paystack-signature: {{paystackSignature}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "event": "charge.success",
    "data": {
      "reference": "abc123ref",
      "status": "success",
      "amount": 90000,
      "customer": {
        "email": "donor@example.com"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "name": "John Doe",
        "comment": "Keep it up"
      }
    }
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Paystack Webhook

  Receives Paystack webhook event notifications. This endpoint is called directly by Paystack's servers when a transaction event occurs (e.g., a successful charge).

  ## Endpoint
  `POST /api/v1/donate/webhook`

  ## Authorization
  Paystack signature verification — the `x-paystack-signature` header must contain a valid HMAC SHA-512 hash of the request body, signed with the Paystack secret key.

  ## Request Headers

  | Header               | Type   | Required | Description                                         |
  | :------------------- | :----- | :------- | :-------------------------------------------------- |
  | x-paystack-signature | string | Yes      | HMAC SHA-512 signature of the JSON payload.          |

  ## Request Body (`JSON`)
  The body is a Paystack event object. The structure varies by event type, but a typical `charge.success` event includes:

  | Field              | Type   | Description                          |
  | :----------------- | :----- | :----------------------------------- |
  | event              | string | Event type (e.g., `charge.success`). |
  | data.reference     | string | Transaction reference.               |
  | data.status        | string | Transaction status.                  |
  | data.amount        | number | Amount in kobo.                      |
  | data.customer      | object | Customer details.                    |
  | data.metadata      | object | Custom metadata (name, comment).     |

  ## Response
  - **Status Code**: `200 OK`
  - Returns immediately to acknowledge receipt.

  ## Error Responses
  - **401 Unauthorized**: Missing or invalid `x-paystack-signature` header.

  ## Notes
  - This endpoint is intended to be called by Paystack servers only — not by clients.
  - The webhook middleware (`verifyPaystackHook`) validates the signature before the controller executes.
}
